5 (|| נָהָר ); compare בַּיָּם אֲשֶׁר הַתַּנִּין 27:1 and בַּיַּמִּים כַּתַּנִּים Ezek 32:2 (simile of Pharaoh); of Euphrates Isa 21:1 ; Jer 51:36 (according to Che Gf and others; Isa 21:1 perhaps better of Persian Gulf, see Di). 7 the great basin in temple-court, called the sea: מוּצָק אֶתהַֿיָּם וַיַּעַשׂ 1Kin 7:23 2Chr 4:2 ; הַנְּחשֶׁת יָם 2Kin 25:13 ; 1Chr 18:8 ; Jer 52:17 ; הַיָּם alone 1Kin 7:24-25 , 10 t. Kings Chronicles + Jer 52:20 . 8 combinations are : a. shore of sea, sea-shore הַיָּם שְׂפַת Josh 11:4 ; 1Kin 5:9 , and in simile Gen 22:17 ; Judg 7:12 ; 1Sam 13:5 ; הַי ׳חוֺף Josh 9:1 ; Ezek 25:16 ; יַמִּים חוֺף Gen 49:13 ; Judg 5:17 ; compare הַיָּם חֶבֶל Zeph 2:5 region by the sea ; so 2:6 but dubious, see I. חֶבֶל 3. b. sand of the sea (shore) הַיָּם חוֺל (in simile) Gen 32:13 ; 41:49 ; Hosea 2:1 ; Isa 10:22 + often (see חוֺל ); לַיָּם גְּבוּל חוֺל Jer 5:22 . c. הַיָּם לְשׁוֺן tongue (arm or gulf) of sea Josh 15:5 ; 18:19 ; Isa 11:5 . d. עַדיָֿם מִיָּם Amos 8:12 ; Zech 9:10 ; Psa 72:8 , compare Micah 7:12 ; Zech 14:8 (twice in verse); Joel 2:20 (twice in verse); Dan 11:45 . 9 = (west, west-word (originally sea-ward , from position of Mediterranean with reference to Palestine, and this sense still often perceptible): with other three points of compass Gen 13:14 ; 28:14 (J), Num 2:18 ; 35:5 (P), Deut 3:27 ; 1Kin 7:25 ; 1Chr 9:24 ; 2Chr 4:4 ; Ezek 42:19 6 t. Ezekiel; Zech 14:4 ; Dan 8:4 ; Psa 107:3 ( וּמִיָּם מִצָּפוֺן וּמִמַּעֲרָב מִמִּזְרָח ; but read perhaps וּמִיָּמִן from the south , Hu Pe Bi Che); opposed to east Josh 11:2 ; 16:6 16t. Ezekiel 48; west alone Gen 12:8 (J); יָם רוּהַ Ezek 10:19 (J) west wind ; לְ מִיָּם westward Josh 8:9 , 12 , 13 +; יָ֫מָּה westward , often of tabernacle Exod 26:22 , 27 ; Num 3:23 +? Josh 5:1 ; 15:8 , 10 etc., + often Ezekiel; הַיָּם דֶּרֶךְ = westward Ezek 41:12 ; יָם גְּבוּל western border Num 34:6 (twice in verse); Josh 15:2 ; מְּאַתיָֿם west side Exod 27:12 ; 38:12 ; Num 35:5 ; Josh 18:14 ; הים דרך מְּאַת Ezek 41:12 (see